{"ts":"2026-07-25T12:28:07.388Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-t5dt4z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Self-reported token accounting: any command can report the token cost of its own output so budget spend is attributable at runtime and in CI"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Token cost is currently measured externally, in a CI corpus gate, against a fixed sample of commands. That answers whether a release regressed on the sampled corpus; it cannot answer where a specific agent's context budget actually went during a real session, which is the question that matters when an agent runs out of context mid-task. Add an opt-in accounting mode in which a command reports the token cost of the output it just produced, decomposed by section — result rows, envelope, diagnostics, hints — using the same tokenizer as the budget contract so the numbers are comparable to the declared ceilings. This makes budget spend attributable at the granularity of a single invocation and lets an agent adapt: if a read cost far more than expected, it can narrow the next one. It also gives the transcript-replay gate real per-command attribution instead of a session total, turning a regression signal into a diagnosis. Accounting must never itself be expensive or on by default: it is opt-in, adds no cost when off, and its own overhead is measured and asserted."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Task"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","area:cli","area:sdk","instrumentation","observability","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-07-25T12:28:07.388Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-25T12:28:07.388Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":300},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"An opt-in accounting mode reports output token cost decomposed by section, using the same tokenizer as the declared budget contract so the figures are directly comparable; Accounting is off by default and adds no measurable cost when off, asserted by a benchmark; The reported figure is asserted equal to an independent count of the emitted bytes, so the accounting cannot drift from reality; Accounting output is itself bounded and excluded from the accounted total, with the exclusion documented; The transcript-replay regression gate consumes per-command accounting so a session regression identifies the responsible commands; Accounting works identically for CLI and MCP transports, since MCP callers pay the same budget"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"project management = context management"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Every token an agent spends is attributable to the command and section that produced it"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Optimizing token cost without per-invocation attribution is guesswork; this converts the whole token-efficiency program from sampling to measurement"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/impact","value":"Adds an opt-in reporting path to the output pipeline; must be provably zero-cost when disabled"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/outcome","value":"A context overrun becomes a diagnosable event with a named cause instead of an unexplained failure"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5oj5"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":70},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-5oj5","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:28:07.388Z"},{"id":"pm-5t33or","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:28:07.388Z"},{"id":"pm-8pnj","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:28:07.388Z"},{"id":"pm-kvxqp1","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-07-25T12:28:07.388Z"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"a761d3bf9d0949bd14a0ee6d13c6de8b87ada9a82599ce3bb01c7bcb057d5cde","message":"File per-invocation token accounting so budget spend becomes attributable rather than sampled"}
